 "answer": "On Windows, Ollama writes its server log to:\n\n**`%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Ollama\\server.log`**\n\nThe full path is usually `C:\\Users\\<your-username>\\AppData\\Local\\Ollama\\server.log`. You can paste `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Ollama` into the File Explorer address bar to open the folder.\n\nThe same folder also contains:\n- **`app.log`**: logs from the Ollama tray application.\n- **`upgrade.log`**: logs from updates.\n\nI believe older server logs are rotated into files such as `server-1.log`, but I'm less certain of the exact naming, so check the folder if you need them. The tray icon's menu also has a \"View logs\" option that opens this folder.",
